    "text": "This is a greedy heuristic, not an optimal solver. At each step it runs Dijkstra from the car's current junction within its remaining time, then picks the unvisited directed street whose length per second of total travel (path plus street) is highest. The cars take turns, always moving the car with the least elapsed time. A 7.5-second wall-clock guard stops the search early. Every committed move is complete, so the output stays valid if it stops early. I have not compiled or run it against any data set.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Edge {\n    int to;\n    long long c;    // time cost\n    long long len;  // length (score)\n    int id;         // street id\n};\n\nint main() {\n    auto startClock = chrono::steady_clock::now();\n    auto timeUp = [&]() {\n        double el = chrono::duration<double>(chrono::steady_clock::now() - startClock).count();\n        return el > 7.5;\n    };\n\n    int N, M;\n    long long T;\n    int C, S;\n    if (!(cin >> N >> M >> T >> C >> S)) return 0;\n\n    // Junction coordinates (unused by the algorithm)\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n        double la, lo;\n        cin >> la >> lo;\n    }\n\n    vector<vector<Edge>> adj(N);\n    vector<long long> eLen(M);\n    for (int j = 0; j < M; j++) {\n        int A, B, D;\n        long long Cc, L;\n        cin >> A >> B >> D >> Cc >> L;\n        eLen[j] = L;\n        adj[A].push_back({B, Cc, L, j});\n        if (D == 2) adj[B].push_back({A, Cc, L, j});\n    }\n\n    vector<char> vis(M, 0);\n    long long score = 0;\n\n    // Per-car state\n    vector<vector<int>> itin(C, vector<int>(1, S));\n    vector<long long> elapsed(C, 0);\n    vector<char> done(C, 0);\n    const long long INF = LLONG_MAX / 4;\n    const size_t MAXV = 1000000;\n\n    vector<long long> dist(N);\n    vector<int> par(N), pedge(N);\n\n    while (true) {\n        if (timeUp()) break;\n\n        // Pick car with minimal elapsed time that is not done\n        int car = -1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < C; i++) {\n            if (done[i]) continue;\n            if (car == -1 || elapsed[i] < elapsed[car]) car = i;\n        }\n        if (car == -1) break;\n\n        int cur = itin[car].back();\n        long long R = T - elapsed[car];\n        if (itin[car].size() >= MAXV) { done[car] = 1; continue; }\n\n        // Dijkstra bounded by remaining time\n        fill(dist.begin(), dist.end(), INF);\n        fill(par.begin(), par.end(), -1);\n        fill(pedge.begin(), pedge.end(), -1);\n        priority_queue<pair<long long, int>, vector<pair<long long, int>>,\n                       greater<pair<long long, int>>> pq;\n        dist[cur] = 0;\n        pq.push({0, cur});\n        while (!pq.empty()) {\n            auto [d, u] = pq.top();\n            pq.pop();\n            if (d != dist[u]) continue;\n            for (const Edge& e : adj[u]) {\n                long long nd = d + e.c;\n                if (nd > R) continue;\n                if (nd < dist[e.to]) {\n                    dist[e.to] = nd;\n                    par[e.to] = u;\n                    pedge[e.to] = e.id;\n                    pq.push({nd, e.to});\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Choose best unvisited directed street to traverse next\n        double bestRatio = -1.0;\n        int bestV = -1, bestIdx = -1;\n        for (int v = 0; v < N; v++) {\n            if (dist[v] >= INF) continue;\n            const auto& lst = adj[v];\n            for (int k = 0; k < (int)lst.size(); k++) {\n                const Edge& e = lst[k];\n                if (vis[e.id]) continue;\n                long long total = dist[v] + e.c;\n                if (total > R) continue;\n                double ratio = (double)e.len / (double)max(total, 1LL);\n                if (ratio > bestRatio) {\n                    bestRatio = ratio;\n                    bestV = v;\n                    bestIdx = k;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (bestV == -1) {\n            done[car] = 1;\n            continue;\n        }\n\n        // Reconstruct path cur -> bestV\n        vector<int> pathNodes;\n        int x = bestV;\n        while (x != cur) {\n            pathNodes.push_back(x);\n            if (!vis[pedge[x]]) {\n                vis[pedge[x]] = 1;\n                score += eLen[pedge[x]];\n            }\n            x = par[x];\n        }\n        reverse(pathNodes.begin(), pathNodes.end());\n\n        const Edge& chosen = adj[bestV][bestIdx];\n        if (itin[car].size() + pathNodes.size() + 1 > MAXV) {\n            done[car] = 1;\n            continue;\n        }\n        for (int v : pathNodes) itin[car].push_back(v);\n\n        // Traverse the chosen street\n        vis[chosen.id] = 1;\n        score += chosen.len;\n        itin[car].push_back(chosen.to);\n        elapsed[car] += dist[bestV] + chosen.c;\n    }\n\n    // Output\n    string out;\n    out.reserve(1 << 20);\n    out += to_string(C);\n    out += '\\n';\n    for (int i = 0; i < C; i++) {\n        out += to_string(itin[i].size());\n        out += '\\n';\n        for (int v : itin[i]) {\n            out += to_string(v);\n            out += '\\n';\n        }\n    }\n    fwrite(out.data(), 1, out.size(), stdout);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
